!! Disk-projection law — see api/disk-projection

The disk-projection law reads: ''a meme resides on disk as one whole carrier — one meme, one file.'' `carrierBaseRelPath` sites every carrier by its lar-URI and returns null for a fragment, so a `#slot` fragment owns no disk file; a child change re-flushes its carrier GROUP through the recompose inverse (`expandMemeRefs` / `exportMemeText`), never its own file. Fragment files MUST NOT appear on any surface a human edits (the grain-leak guard).

The full, load-bearing statement — surfaces, bag roles, projection routing, the disk ward — lives at:

<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/disk-projection#/granularity`>>
